"comparison": "Both BAC and C disclose consolidation policies for agency vs. non-agency mortgage securitizations based on power to direct activities. BAC consolidates agency trusts only when it holds substantially all securities, implying it lacks power to direct activities otherwise. Similarly, C states it does not consolidate U.S. agency-sponsored entities because it lacks the power to direct significant activities. Both firms consolidate non-agency or whole-loan trusts if they act as servicer (possessing power to direct) and hold significant interests.",
