"peer_disclosure_id": "jpm_2024_8_D415",
"relationship": "same_topic",
"comparison": "Both BAC and JPM disclose that servicer status is key to consolidating residential mortgage securitizations. BAC states it generally does not have power to direct activities in agency trusts except when holding substantially all securities, but for whole-loan trusts (including non-agency residential mortgages), it consolidates if it is servicer and holds significant interests. JPM explicitly states it does not consolidate residential mortgage securitizations if it is not the servicer (and thus lacks power to direct activities) or does not hold a potentially significant beneficial interest.",
