"peer_disclosure_id": "jpm_2024_8_D417",
"relationship": "same_topic",
"comparison": "Both BAC and JPM describe the distribution of power in commercial mortgage securitization trusts. BAC states that power to direct significant activities in commercial mortgage trusts is typically held by the special servicer or the party holding specific subordinate securities with controlling rights. JPM similarly states that for commercial mortgage securitizations, the power to direct significant activities is generally held by the servicer or investors in a specified controlling class of securities. Both note that the reporting entity (BAC/JPM) generally does not hold the controlling interest that grants this power.",
