"comparison": "Both BAC and MS define servicing as the primary source of power to direct significant activities in securitizations, leading to consolidation if significant interests are held. BAC states that when it is the servicer of whole loans (including non-agency residential mortgages), it has the power to direct the most significant activities and consolidates if it also holds significant interests. MS states that servicing decisions represent the power to make the most significant economic decisions and that it consolidates securitizations where it acts as servicer and holds a potentially significant interest.",
